From: Grant McNaught <1371263+gmcnaught@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 16:50:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 31/35] fix(render): emit static tile-list after animated ops,
 not before

Entities.cpp's FAST draw path put the static (non-animated) tile-list
replay BEFORE the layer's animated-tile op loop, on the assumption that
the static bucket only holds tiles spatially disjoint from any animated
tile (NonAnimatedRegions::build's overlaps_animated_tile check), so draw
order between the two groups doesn't matter.

That assumption holds for ordinary animated decorations (torches, water)
but not for a self-scrolling/parallax pattern (scroll_ratio != 1): its
on-screen position is camera-relative, not fixed to its declared
map-space box, so at runtime it can cover static tiles the build-time
overlap check classified as disjoint. With static-first order, a
parallax 'distant background' pattern was painting in front of the rest
of its own layer instead of behind it.

Swap the call order back to animated-then-static, matching the engine's
original per-cell compositing order (animated tiles, then a holed
non-animated cell painted on top). Zero cost -- it's the same two calls,
reordered.
---
 src/entities/Entities.cpp | 24 ++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/entities/Entities.cpp b/src/entities/Entities.cpp
index 0f42d3b..f5b3c0c 100644
--- a/src/entities/Entities.cpp
+++ b/src/entities/Entities.cpp
@@ -1522,20 +1522,28 @@ void Entities::draw() {
                             pat->get_current_frame(), fc, fr);
         }
       }
+      // [static tile-list] Animated ops emitted BEFORE the static layer, matching the
+      // original per-cell order (animated first, then a holed non-animated cell on top).
+      // The static bucket only ever holds tiles that DON'T overlap any animated tile's
+      // declared map-space square (NonAnimatedRegions::build/overlaps_animated_tile) --
+      // for ordinary animated decorations (torches, water) that disjointness makes the
+      // two orders equivalent. It does NOT hold for a self-scrolling/parallax pattern
+      // (scroll_ratio != 1): its on-screen position is camera-relative, not fixed to its
+      // declared map-space box, so at runtime it can cover static tiles the build-time
+      // overlap check classified as disjoint. Emitting it after static (as before) let a
+      // parallax "distant background" paint in FRONT of the rest of its own layer instead
+      // of behind it. Static-after-animated restores the vanilla result: static content
+      // occludes the background wherever it's placed, and the background only shows
+      // through the gaps -- with zero cost, since this is just a call-order swap.
+      const int _nops = R.resident_layer_op_count(layer);
+      for (int _oi = 0; _oi < _nops; ++_oi) R.resident_emit_layer_op(layer, _oi);
       if (_tilestatic) {
-        // [static tile-list] Emitted BEFORE the animated op loop so animated tiles paint on
-        // top of this background -- the reverse of the original per-cell order (animated
-        // first, then a holed non-animated cell on top); putting static first and letting
-        // animated overpaint it gets the same result without per-cell hole-punching.
         // [Phase 3b] One call replaces the per-op replay loop: the renderer decides
         // internally whether to emit a single windowed COPY from a baked background
         // plane or fall back to replaying every static bucket (resident_static_op_count/
-        // resident_emit_static_op), so paint order relative to the animated op loop below
-        // is unchanged either way.
+        // resident_emit_static_op).
         R.resident_emit_static_layer(layer);
       }
-      const int _nops = R.resident_layer_op_count(layer);
-      for (int _oi = 0; _oi < _nops; ++_oi) R.resident_emit_layer_op(layer, _oi);
     }
     else {
       // BUILD (rmode==1) or disabled (rmode==0): walk the animated tiles. In BUILD the
